Jamie Harrison was doing well by raising a

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:03.590
million and a half dollars in general against
Lindsay Graham, Amy McGrath has raised two

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:07.470
and a half million in 24 hours.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:12.260
And the McGrath campaign is claiming, and
at least for now, I haven't been able to find

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.610
conflicting information.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:18.120
The McGrath campaign claims that two and a
half million bucks in the first 24 hours is

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.690
a record for the first 24 hours of any senate
campaign period, which sort of sounds like

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:29.100
a big claim, but I researched it this morning
and I was not able to find anything to contradict

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.100
it.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.270
A average donation to Amy McGrath is about
$36.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:38.390
The 2.5 million does not include money that
was sent in via check checks written during

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.670
the first 24 hours, but which will of course
not be received for another couple of days.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:48.270
Um, and money, uh, also pledged, but not yet
given which I don't know exactly.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.870
Maybe at fundraisers money can be pledged,
